### Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe the problem.

I created a new .Net 9.0 preview 6 Blazor Web App with the global Auto interactivity mode.
I applied the content security policies from the [documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/aspnet/core/blazor/security/content-security-policy?view=aspnetcore-9.0#client-side-blazor-apps) adding what's needed for local development:

```html
    <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy"
          content="base-uri 'self';
                default-src 'self';
                img-src data: https:;
                object-src 'none';
                script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval';
                style-src 'self';
                upgrade-insecure-requests;
                connect-src 'self' ws://localhost:* http://localhost:* "> <!-- For local development -->
```

Chrome and Firefox refuse to execute the importmap inline script because it is not allowed by the content security policy.

### Describe the solution you'd like

Add a new nullable string parameter to the ImportMap componet for specifying a Nonce and use it to create a nonce attribute on the importmap script tag:

```csharp
public sealed class ImportMap : IComponent
{
	\\...
	
	[Parameter] public string? Nonce { get; set; }
	
	\\...

	private void RenderImportMap(RenderTreeBuilder builder)
	{
		builder.OpenElement(0, "script");
		builder.AddAttribute(1, "type", "importmap");

		if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Nonce))
		{
			builder.AddAttribute(2, "nonce", Nonce);
		}

		builder.AddMarkupContent(3, _computedImportMapDefinition!.ToJson());
		builder.CloseElement();
	}
}
```

