comments:
@ghidello thanks for contacting us.

I've created a PR with a fix https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/57282 so that the additional parameters can be passed down to the script tag.

That said, there's (in my opinion) a better alternative. You can grab the `ImportMapDefinition` from endpoint metadata, compute the sha256 hash and add that to the CSP policy instead of using the nonce.

```
HttpContext?.GetEndpoint()?.Metadata.GetMetadata<ImportMapDefinition>();
```
